# The ShellCheck release the gate accepts, pinned. One version, here and
# nowhere else: the ci workflow reads this file, and CONTRIBUTING.md and
# docs/dev.md point at it rather than restating a number.
#
# ShellCheck is neither a crates.io package nor a Go program, so it cannot sit
# in .github/cargo-tools or .github/go-tools beside the rest. This file holds a
# bare release the way .bun-version does, and the ci workflow joins the tool
# name onto it to build the coordinate its installer takes.
#
# actionlint runs ShellCheck over a `run:` block whose shell it resolves to sh
# or bash, when it finds the analyzer on PATH, and says nothing at all when it
# does not. The gate holds the installed release equal to this line before it
# runs actionlint, so both continuous integration legs check the same thing.
#
# Nothing bumps this automatically. Dependabot has no ecosystem for a release
# pinned in a bare file, so a human edits it.
0.11.0
